{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1395889-m20-featering-sorcerers","id":1395889,"title":"M20 featering Sorcerers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-11T12:52:55-07:00","id":1395889,"title":"M20 featering Sorcerers","content":"As there is from my knowing nothing in the V20 and W20 books, does M20 have book which contains sorcery rules or do I need for it an older book hoping that it whas translated back then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T13:42:07-07:00","id":1395904,"title":"","content":"There are not official sorcery, aka linear magic, rules in M20.<br /> <br /> That being said, if you want a Storyteller's vault product, there is Sorceror's Companion, which will convert the prior WOD Sorcerer Revised material to M20 and add a few more options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/259124/Sorcerers-Companion\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/259124.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/259124/Sorcerers-Companion\" target=\"_blank\"> Sorcerer's Companion - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/259124/Sorcerers-Companion\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/259124/Sorcerers-Companion </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Sorcerer's Companion - The Sorcerer's Companion provides new options for Players and advice for Storytellers of Sorcerer games utilizing Sorcer </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T13:48:13-07:00","id":1395905,"title":"","content":"V20's Hunters Hunted II, and W20's Kinfolk A Breed Apart, don't have the full rules that something like the Sorcerer books do, or the STV book above, but do have official Numina rules for 20th books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T13:56:32-07:00","id":1395907,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114261/V20-The-Hunters-Hunted-II\" target=\"_blank\"><i>The Hunters Hunted II</i></a> for V20 has rules on Hedge Magic and other Numina. It's not nearly as comprehensive as the Sorcerer books for Mage are, but at least it gives you a few paths designed to work in 20tth edition games.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}